  "texts": {
    "preamble": "C.Vinothkumar vs The State Of Tamil Nadu on 26 September, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.No.11856 of In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 26.09.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.No. 11856 of 2016 and Wmp No. 10227 of 2016 C.Vinothkumar ... Petition Vs. 1.The State of Tamil Nadu, Rep. by its Principal Secretary to Government, Municipal Administration & Water Supply Department, Secretariat, Fort St.George, Chennai - 600 009. 2.The Commissioner, Chennai Corporation, Ribbon Building, Chennai - 600 003. 3.Thiru.Kannan, Deputy Commissioner, Chennai Corporation, Ribbon Building, Chennai - 600 003. 4.Dr .Saraswathi, Additional Health Officer (Central Zone), Chennai Corporation, Ribbon Building, Chennai - 600 003. 1/5 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P.N C.Vinothkumar vs The State Of Tamil Nadu on 26 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/103275310/ 1 5.The Zonal Health Officer, Chennai Corporation, Zone Vi, Ayanavaram, Chennai - 600 023. 6.The Food Safety Commissioner, Dms Compound, V Floor, Teynampet, Chennai - 600 006. ... R (R6 - is suo-motu impleaded as per order dated 07.04.2016 by TSSJ in WP.No.11856/2016) PRAYER: Writ Petition is filed under Article 226 of the Constitutio India, to issue a Writ of Mandamus, directing the 1st and 2nd respo take appropriate legal action against the officials concerned for h forcibly removed the food articles from the petitioner's premises o 16.03.2016 in contravention of law and consequently directing the respondents to return the food articles to the petitioner. For Petitioner : Mr.S.Nedunchezhiyan For Respondent : Mr.S.Jayachandran Government Advocate for R1 & R6 Mrs.K.Aswini Devi Standing Counsel for R2 & R5 ** ** * * * 2/5 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W ORDER This learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submitted that the prayer in the Writ Petition has become infructuous and hence, nothing survives for further adjudication.",
